There exists a countable universe $U$ and a countable language collection
$\cC\subseteq 2^U$ such that every language in $\cC$ admits a finite
tell-tale set and the following holds. Define
\begin{align}
 \bar{\cP}(\cC)=\cP_{Opt}(\cC)\setminus \cP(\cC)
 =
 \{\cD \in \cP_{Opt}(\cC) :
 \forall L \in \optarg_{\cD,\cC},\
 \forall T_L\in \cT_L,\ T_L\not\subseteq \supp(\cD)\}.
\label{eq:necessity-supported-tell-tales-1}
\end{align}
Then, for every deterministic identification algorithm $\bar{\cA}$, there exists
$\cD\in\bar{\cP}(\cC)$ such that
\begin{align*}
\liminf_{n\to \infty}
\p_{\rS \sim \cD^n}\left[
L_{\bar{\cA}(\rS)}\in \optarg_{\cD,\cC},\
\not\exists L\in\optarg_{\cD,\cC}
\text{ such that }L\subsetneq L_{\bar{\cA}(\rS)}
\right]
\leq \frac{1}{2}.
\end{align*}

