\end{align}

quotes.tex:
Fix any $ 0<\eps <1$. There exists a countable universe $U$, such that for any generation algorithm $ \cA $ using randomness $\rr$, there exists a distribution $ \cD $ over $U$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \generr(\cA, \cD, n) \geq 1-\eps.
    \end{align*}

